      "updated_at": "2026-05-20T11:52:55Z",
      "body": "> It might be a good idea to address this with better documentation then. Since you encountered this, can I ask where you could have expected to pick up on something like this?\n\nThis might be a strange/bad place to put that documentation, but I landed on [the docs for `memory_cleanup`](https://docs.rs/burn/latest/burn/prelude/trait.Backend.html#method.memory_cleanup) when I was first trying to figure this out. Regardless of where the documentation goes, something along these lines may have clued me in:\n\n> The `Autodiff<B>` backend retains ops until a `backward()` pass passes through them. Ops that are never touched by a backward pass are _never_ cleaned up, and should instead be performed on the inner backend `B`.\n\nEdit: I'm not entirely sure of how accurate the wording in the above description is. Is it only the parameters themselves that have something left over, not the ops?",
